e back )TjT*-0.006 Tw(panel. When a plug is inserted into the associated Submix jack on the back )TjT*0 Tw(panel, the )Tj/F20 1 Tf4.962 0 TD[(Dr)-12(y por)-8(tion of the Send is disconnected)]TJ/F17 1 Tf19.589 0 TD( from the effects )Tj-24.55 -1.2 TD(processor and the signal is routed directly to the output jack. The actual )TjT*-0.044 Tw[(output routing is shown in parentheses in the display)74(. If you don\325)18(t want the )]TJT*0 Tw(wet portion of the signal in the main mix, turn down the Send Level. )Tj/F21 1 TfT*[(The Dr)-12(y Send is disconnected fr)8(om the Effects Pr)8(ocessors even if only one plug is )]TJT*[(inser)-10(ted into the Submix jack.)]TJ/F17 1 Tf0 -2.1 TD(The four Effect Sends allow you to get the most out of the two effect )Tj0 -1.2 TD(processors. For example, with Effect B set to an echo algorithm, you could )TjT*(route one MIDI channel to Send 3 and set the effect amount to 80%. )TjT*(Another MIDI channel could be routed to Send 4 with an effect amount of )TjT*(only 5%. This is almost like having two different effects! )Tj0 -2.1 TD(The Mix Output function is also useful when sequencing since it lets you )Tj0 -1.2 TD(route speci\336c MIDI channels \(and thus sequencer tracks\) to speci\336c Sub )TjT*(outputs \(on the back panel\) where there they can be processed with EQ or )TjT*(other outboard effects.)Tj/F24 1 Tf14 0 0 14 262 571.809 Tm(channel 16:  Send2->main)TjET253.974 608.335 256.675 -46.758 reSBT14 0 0 14 263 590.309 Tm(MIX OUTPUT)TjET249 613.309 265.629 -56.707 re415.268 554.508 m411.797 554.508 l415.268 566.613 l418.739 554.508 ls415.268 554.508 m411.797 554.508 l415.268 566.613 l418.739 554.508 lf*415.268 554.008 m415.268 544 lSBT/F23 1 Tf9 0 0 9 364.237 534.182 Tm[(Indicates that the dr)-12(y signal is)]TJ-0.674 -1 TD(routed to the Main output jacks.)Tj/F24 1 Tf14 0 0 14 262 361.758 Tm(channel 15:  use preset)TjET0 J 253.974 398.283 256.675 -46.758 reS